# 2. LOCATION-BASED EXPERIENCE

Use the user's selected/available location at an appropriate privacy level.

Do NOT expose exact user location publicly.

Use levels such as:

* City
* Region
* Country

Example:

"Pune users"

"Mumbai users"

"People in Maharashtra"

"India"

Do not display exact GPS coordinates, home address, building, street, or precise location.

Questions may be personalized based on city.

Example:

For Pune:

"What matters more when choosing a weekend plan?"

A. Cafe hopping
B. Trekking
C. Movies
D. Staying home

The result could show:

"63% of Pune users chose the same answer."

Only show city-level statistics when there is sufficient sample size. Establish a configurable minimum sample threshold to avoid exposing statistics about very small groups.

